---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-container</code> centres page content and caps its width, so lines stay readable on
  wide screens. <code>size</code> picks the maximum width from the container tokens:
  <code>sm</code> (320px), <code>md</code> (672px), <code>lg</code> (1056px), <code>xl</code>
  (1312px) or <code>max</code> (1584px). The default, <code>full</code>, has no maximum.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; border: 1px dashed var(--color-outline-variant);'>
    <wc-container size='sm'>
      <wc-card variant='outlined'>
        <wc-card-content>This content is at most 320px wide and centred.</wc-card-content>
      </wc-card>
    </wc-container>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Layout</h3>
<p>
  The container only sets the width. Put a <code>wc-stack</code> or <code>wc-grid</code> inside it
  to arrange the content, and use <code>wc-app-shell</code> for the frame of a whole app.
  <code>--container-max-width</code> overrides the width and <code>--container-padding</code> the
  space at the sides.
</p>
